# Coding Style

## Vue Components

- Always use `<script setup lang="ts">`
- No Options API
- Props and emits must be typed
- Keep components presentational; call Engine for mutations

```vue
<script setup lang="ts">
import { engineAdvanceTurn } from '@engine/index'
import { useGameState } from '@state/useGameState'

const gameState = useGameState()

function handleAdvance(): void {
  engineAdvanceTurn()
}
</script>
```

## TypeScript

- TypeScript everywhere; no `.js` source files
- Use `interface` for object shapes, `type` for unions/aliases
- Avoid classes unless wrapping a third-party library
- Prefer named exports over default exports (except Vue SFCs)

## Imports

Use path aliases: `@engine/`, `@state/`, `@ui/`, `@data/`, `@/types`

## Naming

- Engine actions: `engineAdvanceTurn`, `engineSpawnCharacter` (exported from `src/engine/index.ts`)
- Engine internals: `advanceTurn`, `spawnFromTemplate` (domain verbs)
- Pinia stores: `useUiStore`, `use<Name>Store`
- Types: PascalCase nouns (`GameState`, `ItemDefinition`)

## Files

- One primary export per Engine module
- Colocate component styles with `<style scoped>`
- JSON content uses kebab-case filenames
